## Why This Is Asked
This probes end-to-end streaming design under regulatory constraints, balancing latency, security, and reliability across on-prem and GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Exactly-once streaming with Pub/Sub and Dataflow
- CMEK on Pub/Sub and BigQuery
- Private connectivity and VPC Service Controls
- IAM least privilege and service accounts
- Idempotent sinks and dedupe strategies
- Dead-lettering, replay protection, and failure handling
- Cost considerations (throughput, windowing, autoscaling)

## Code Example
```java
// Pseudo-beam snippet: read from Pub/Sub, map to BigQuery rows, write with schema
Pipeline p = Pipeline.create(options);
PCollection<TableRow> rows = p.apply("ReadPubSub", PubsubIO.readMessagesWithAttributes().fromTopic("projects/PROJECT/topics/TOPIC"))
  .apply("ToBQRow", ParDo.of(new DoFn<PubsubMessage, TableRow>() {
     @ProcessElement
     public void process(@Element PubsubMessage m, OutputReceiver<TableRow> out) {
        TableRow row = parseToTableRow(m);
        out.output(row);
     }
  }));
rows.apply(BigQueryIO.writeTableRows().to("PROJECT:DATASET.TABLE").withSchema(schema)
  .withCreateDisposition(CreateDisposition.CREATE_IF_NEEDED)
  .withWriteDisposition(WriteDisposition.WRITE_APPEND);
p.run();
```

